# Copy to .env (gitignored) only when this working copy must differ from the defaults.
#
# This repo is cloned more than once on the Mac Mini (VSC-ACADEMY, VSC-ACADEMY-hardening, agent
# worktrees). Every copy shares the committed docker-compose.yml, so the committed values can only
# hold ONE port set. A second copy that runs its own backend must claim its own ports here —
# otherwise `docker compose up` fails on "port is already allocated", or worse, both copies share
# the same compose project name and therefore the SAME Docker volume, overwriting each other's data.
#
# Pick free ports from ~/ops/docs/convex-ports.md and add your copy to the table there.
# Check a candidate port BOTH ways — a port reserved by a project that is currently stopped does
# not show up in lsof:
#     lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN | grep -E ':(3322|6807)$'
#     grep -rn '127.0.0.1:3322:' ~/projects ~/ops/infra --include=docker-compose.yml
#
# Committed defaults (used when this file is absent) = the VSC-ACADEMY reservation:
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_PROJECT=vsc-academy-convex
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_INSTANCE=vsc-academy-local
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_PORT=3320
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_SITE_PORT=3321
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_DASHBOARD_PORT=6800
#
# Example — the VSC-ACADEMY-hardening copy:
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_PROJECT=vsc-academy-hardening-convex
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_INSTANCE=vsc-academy-hardening-local
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_PORT=3322
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_SITE_PORT=3323
#     ACADEMY_CONVEX_DASHBOARD_PORT=6807
#
# ACADEMY_CONVEX_PROJECT must be unique per copy: it is the Docker compose project name, and the
# volume is named after it. Two copies sharing it share one database.
#
# Never use 3280/3281/6796 — those belong to teduenglish, which is running.
